From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Report a refused directory scan on ps5.

find_file_in_dir's case-insensitive search is the only caller of
pw_cwd_scan_directory, so when that call breaks nothing else notices: a
prefix written in lower case reaches the search only for a name spelled
some other way, and then every such lookup fails at once. That is how
readdir failing on /data went unseen until a 32-bit game asked for its
imports exactly as its import table spells them and GTA IV lost all
twenty-one of them to c0000135.

Report a refusal, with the directory, the name and errno. Not a miss: a
name that is simply not in the directory is the ordinary answer -- the
loader looks in the game's own folder first -- and reporting those spends
the budget before anything interesting happens. The cap is 32.

This also says whether a DLL load ending in STATUS_NO_MEMORY took it from
here or from somewhere further in.

Diagnostic only; no behaviour changes.
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index ec35dea354..46bf0d69bc 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -3177,6 +3177,23 @@ static NTSTATUS find_file_in_dir( int root_fd, char *unix_name, int pos, const W
     match.length = length;
     match.is_name_8_dot_3 = is_name_8_dot_3;
     ret = pw_cwd_scan_directory( root_fd, unix_name, match_dir_entry, &match, &flags );
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. Only a refusal, never a miss: a name that is simply not in
+     * the directory is the ordinary answer here -- the loader looks for every
+     * dll in the game's own folder first -- and reporting those spends the
+     * budget before anything interesting happens. A refusal is different: this
+     * search is the only caller, so when it breaks, every lookup that needs a
+     * name spelled some other way fails at once and nothing else notices.
+     * errno names which, and whether a DLL load that ends in STATUS_NO_MEMORY
+     * got it from here or from somewhere further in. */
+    {
+        static int reported;
+        if (ret < 0 && reported < 32)
+        {
+            reported++;
+            ERR( "ps5 scan refused: dir %s want %s -> errno %d (root_fd %d)\n",
+                 debugstr_a(unix_name), debugstr_wn(name, length), errno, root_fd );
+        }
+    }
     if (ret < 0) return errno_to_status( errno );
     if (ret > 0)
     {
